    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Beautifully appointed one-bedroom apartment in the prestigious Thornwood development, ideally located just off Booterstown Avenue.\r\n\r\nCombining contemporary design with generous proportions, this superb second-floor apartment extends to approximately 55.4 sq m (596 sq. ft) and enjoys a prime location close to a wealth of local amenities.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hall leading to a spacious open-plan living/dining area, flooded with natural light from an expansive floor-to-ceiling window. The space is complemented by a fully fitted kitchen complete with integrated appliances. The double bedroom is generously proportioned and bright, featuring fitted wardrobes and direct access to the balcony. A separate utility room, a fully tiled bathroom, and a convenient storage press complete the accommodation. The property is further enhanced by a west-facing balcony, accessible from both the living area and the bedroom, providing an ideal space for relaxation.\r\n\r\nDesigned by O’Mahony Pike Architects, Thornwood is an award-winning development that comprises 152 apartments, four townhouses, and eight penthouses, all arranged around meticulously landscaped communal courtyards. Booterstown is a highly sought-after south Dublin suburb, perfectly positioned between Blackrock, Mount Merrion and Stillorgan, providing a wide range of shopping, dining, and leisure amenities. The picturesque Blackrock Village is just a short distance away, offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, and boutiques, along with the beautiful Blackrock Park and scenic coastal walk stretching from Blackrock towards Seapoint and Dún Laoghaire.\r\nThere are numerous sports amenities in the area, with a choice of golf clubs, tennis, rugby clubs and UCD sports centre all nearby. Transport links are exceptional, with Booterstown DART Station close by and QBC routes along the N11 and Rock Road."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation: \r\nEntrance Hall (3.273m x 1.34m): Welcoming entrance hall with laminate wood floor and recessed lighting.\r\nMain Bedroom (4.0m x 3.21m): Spacious main bedroom with laminate wood floor and recessed lighting, and a built-in wardrobe and access to the balcony. \r\nLiving Room (46.78m x 3.59m): Generous living/dining room with floor-to-ceiling windows, laminate wood floor and recessed lighting. \r\nKitchen (2.29 m x 1.82 m): Contemporary kitchen with granite countertops, integrated appliances, tiled floor and recessed lighting. \r\nUtility Room (1.82 m x 1.19 m): Practical utility space with washer-dryer and ample storage. \r\nBathroom (2.27mx1.71m): Fully tiled bathroom with w.c., w.h.b. and bath with shower, heated towel rail, recessed lighting and extractor fan \r\nBalcony (3.28mx1.66m): West facing balcony"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tBright and spacious 2nd-floor apartment \r\n•\tApprox. 55.4 sq.m. / 596 sq.ft. \r\n•\tBER B3\r\n•\tNo Rent Cap\r\n•\tWest-facing aspect\r\n•\tContemporary fully fitted kitchen with integrated appliances \r\n•\tUtility Room \r\n•\tGas-Fired Central Heating \r\n•\tDesignated underground parking space \r\n•\tConvenient location close to local amenities \r\n•\tAward-winning development (Opus Award, 2007) \r\n•\tLandscaped communal grounds\r\n•\tExcellent transport links (DART and QBC) \r\n•\tManagement Company: Indigo Real Estate Management Company. 2025/2026 Service charge approx. €2,200."
      },
